in the last decades of the british  empire and during the decolonization era  people from the former british colonies  still came to study at the university of  oxford as it was one of the most  advanced universities in the former  empire however this fact was a  contentious subject in the colonies  because oxford along with other english  universities of the time was by design  the place where the empire's elite and  top scholars came to study resulting in  the fact that colonial schools were  often neglected and underdeveloped  bandaranaike who later became the leader  of the sri lankan freedom party came to  study at oxford and he observed that for  all the benefits an oxford education  gives a person these are not outweighed  by the negatives of taking people from  the colonies to be educated in england  rather than in their own countries jk  chetter an indian poet who was at oxford  at the same time disagreed with this  opinion saying that the centralization  of all the brightest people in one place  was a good thing if you want to know  more check out my video on it on the  mlaser history youtube channel
 

